From: CoreELEC Xiaomi SMB3 Multichannel laboratory
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL MINIMAL-R2] cifs: backport final secondary-channel hostname handling

Runtime evidence R19 v7 showed every secondary cifs_get_tcp_session()
attempt returning ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM) before socket creation.

This backport reproduces the final upstream behavior obtained after:
  5112d80c162f456b3956dd4f5c58e9f0c6498516 cifs: populate server_hostname for extra channels
  4c14d7043fede258957d7b01da0cad2d9fe3a205 cifs: populate empty hostnames for extra channels

The final state uses an allocated empty hostname for secondary channels
and skips hostname DNS refresh for that empty value during reconnect.

--- a/fs/cifs/sess.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/sess.c
@@ -223,6 +223,9 @@
 	/* Auth */
 	ctx.domainauto = ses->domainAuto;
 	ctx.domainname = ses->domainName;
+
+	/* no hostname for extra channels */
+	ctx.server_hostname = "";
 	ctx.username = ses->user_name;
 	ctx.password = ses->password;
 	ctx.sectype = ses->sectype;
--- a/fs/cifs/connect.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/connect.c
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@
 	if (!server->hostname)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* if server hostname isn't populated, there's nothing to do here */
+	if (server->hostname[0] == '\0')
+		return 0;
+
 	len = strlen(server->hostname) + 3;
 
 	unc = kmalloc(len, GFP_KERNEL);
